# ── Everything goes through the API gateway ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Deployed: vercel.json rewrites the relative paths this app calls to the
# gateway, which authenticates, meters and routes them to the real service.
# The browser only ever talks to this app's own origin, so CORS never applies.
#
#     https://api-gateway-two-nu.vercel.app
#
# That is why the VITE_* base URLs below stay EMPTY. Setting one bakes an
# absolute URL into the bundle, so the browser calls that host directly and
# bypasses the gateway entirely — no auth enforcement, no metering, no budgets,
# and the target service then needs this app's origin in its CORS allowlist.
# Leave them unset unless you are deliberately bypassing the gateway.
#
# Local dev: the Vite proxy in vite.config.ts forwards the same paths. Point it
# at a locally running gateway (port 8000) to exercise the same path, or at the
# individual services to work on one in isolation.

# Base URL of a deployed knowledge-service instance.
# Leave unset in local dev — the Vite proxy forwards /v1/* to
# http://localhost:8090 (see vite.config.ts).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional: a knowledge-service API key (KNOWLEDGE_API_KEYS on that service),
# sent as `X-API-Key` on every request. Required once that service has
# KNOWLEDGE_API_KEYS or RAG_AUTH_ENABLED configured — leave unset for a local
# instance with neither set (open/dev mode).
# The stats card (GET /v1/stats) needs a key whose role is "admin"
# (KNOWLEDGE_API_KEYS format: name:key:admin) — a "user"-role key can still
# upload/query/browse files, it just can't see the stats card.
VITE_API_KEY=

# Remember: the target knowledge-service must also set
# KNOWLEDGE_CORS_ORIGINS to include this app's origin (e.g.
# http://localhost:5174) — CORS is off by default (service-to-service only).

# Base URL of a deployed auth-service instance (sign-in/sign-up for this UI).
# Leave unset in local dev — the Vite proxy forwards /auth/* to
# http://localhost:8100 (see vite.config.ts).
# NOTE: this token is ALSO sent as a Bearer header on every knowledge-service
# request (see api/client.ts) — for it to be accepted there (and for
# org_id/user_id to be derived from it instead of the request body), the
# target knowledge-service must have RAG_AUTH_ENABLED=true with
# RAG_JWT_SECRET/RAG_JWT_ISSUER matching this auth-service's
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET/AUTH_JWT_ISSUER. Leaving VITE_API_KEY (above) set on a
# deployment that also does per-user login defeats this — see that var's note.
VITE_AUTH_BASE_URL=

# The target auth-service must also set AUTHSVC_CORS_ORIGINS to include this
# app's origin (e.g. http://localhost:5174) — same default-closed CORS
# policy as knowledge-service.
